US-030 is implemented and verified on Windows and the Linux build/test presets, with one open item: the native Linux Vulkan GPU run. This WSL host has no Vulkan device that meets the engine's requirements, so that suite reports not-run and the story is not complete. I did not emit the completion signal.

**What was already there:** Most of the Vulkan resource model was already in the tree: CpuWrite/CpuRead staging buffers, descriptor sets and pools, fence-deferred retirement, synchronization2 barriers, and capability checks before pipeline creation and indirect-count draws.

**What I fixed:** The Vulkan GPU suite failed 5 swapchain cases on Windows (the failure US-038 left open). `VulkanSwapchain::recreate` moved every back-buffer image to PRESENT_SRC before any acquire, which the 1.4.363 validation layer rejects.
- Images now start UNDEFINED.
- `present()` moves an acquired image that nothing has transitioned into PRESENT_SRC, inside the frame-sync submission that already waits on the acquire.
- If a list consumed the acquire without touching that image, `present()` returns a StateMismatch error instead of presenting it in an invalid layout.
- `VulkanDevice::submit_frame_syncs` takes an optional record callback to support this.

**Gate results on the final tree:**
- **Windows:** ValidateVendor, win-dev, and win-debug pass with zero compile errors. win-unit passes (21/21). DX12 GPU passes (40/40). Vulkan GPU passes (41/41) with validation layers on, on the RTX 5080.
- **Linux:** ValidateVendor, linux-dev, and linux-debug pass with zero errors or warnings. linux-unit passes (22/22). linux-asan builds, and linux-sanitize passes (22/22). linux-gcc builds with zero errors or warnings, and linux-gcc-unit passes (22/22).

